            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0108" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 46.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By cable.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 21, 1870</date>—10.50 a. m.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Government refuses to exempt North German steamers from capture, except those now
                    at sea, ignorant of war, which may enter French port.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
